  "body": "TestAgyTitleLater went red in a full run here, at 393801bc on top of 098ac969:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestAgyTitleLater (0.01s)\n    agy_test.go:122: title after agy renamed it: \"Listing the folder\"\n```\n\nOn origin/main e5dd8696 alone it's red 2 of 200 (`go test -tags nogui -count=200 -run '^TestAgyTitleLater$' ./internal/sessions/`, Linux 5.15, go1.26.8).\n\nagySummariesOf reads conversation_summaries.db again only when its mtime or size changed. The test's UPDATE rewrites a page in place, so the size stays the same, and Linux stamps mtime from its coarse clock (4ms here, CONFIG_HZ=250). When the UPDATE lands in the same tick as putAgy's writes, the rev doesn't change and the old title stays. Setting the db's mtime back to its time before the UPDATE (os.Chtimes) makes it red 3 of 3 with the same message.\n\nA user can hit this too: if agy writes a title in the same tick as a write magpie has already read, the new title doesn't show until the db changes again. CI's ubuntu runners have the same coarse mtime.\n\nI'll take it. The plan is git's \"racily clean\" rule: don't keep a rev whose mtime is that close to the read, so the next list reads the db again.\n",
