   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3708-agy-settle` (head `1c8f94de`, on upstream `6afbe3f3`) — an agy summary database written within the settle window is read again next time.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/sessions/agy.go`'s `agySummariesOf` built its revision from mtime-nanos plus size and reused the cached rows when the string matched. A write that lands in the same mtime tick with the same size looks unchanged, which is the 2-in-200 red the report saw.\n\n**Change.** a settle rule: rows read from a database written within `agySettle` are served but their revision is not kept, so the next look re-reads (git's racily-clean rule); a settled database is still cached, and a test pins both halves.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/sessions/ -run TestAgySummariesSettle` → `agy_settle_test.go:50: a title written in the settle window: \"Listing the folder\"`\nGreen: `PASS, plus `TestAgyTitleLater` 20/20 and the package's tests` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions`\n\n`internal/sessions/revision_cache.go` has the same mtime+size shape and its own recent-window rule already; I did not fold the two together.\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 26's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6afbe3f3` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3708-agy-settle — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
