     "body": "My patch for #3708 adds `filememo.Settled`: a stamp of a file's size and time isn't reused until the file's time is 2s old. Linux stamps a file from a clock a few ms coarse, so a second write of the same size inside that tick leaves both as they were, and whatever was read before keeps showing until the next write.\n\nThese keep what they read by such a stamp the same way, with no time limit (lines at 1bb8143b).\n\ninternal/sessions:\n- `ocStamp` (calls_opencode.go:67): OpenCode's and ZCode's call lists, and WorkBuddy's models.json (`buddyGatewayIDs`)\n- `hermesRevision` (hermes.go:91)\n- `pollOpenCode`'s stamp (traces_opencode.go:74)\n- Cline's carry (cline.go:148)\n- `cursorStamp` (cursor_snapshot.go:44). A new copy for each look while the store's time is that recent would bring #1988 back, so this one needs another way.\n- the parse `refresh` keeps for each session file (sessions.go:914), for an agent that rewrites its session file whole. A file that is only appended to can't keep its size.\n\nElsewhere:\n- proc/look.go:134 is #3141.\n- proc/version.go:38: a CLI whose `--version` failed isn't run again.\n- the plugin loaders' stamps, agentplug/agentplug.go:200 and middleware/middleware.go:150, and plugin/store.go:287's `listStamp` under both.\n- omarchy/omarchy.go:367, the theme.\n- usage's `statKey` (request_page.go:600), in the request page's and the summary's keys. #1305 gave the usage log's own stamp a settle rule; these have none.\n\nTwo keep theirs for a while only, so a missed write shows up later: agent/cliupdate.go:584 (a CLI's version, up to a day) and provider/vertex.go:298 (a Vertex token, until it nearly lapses). Two already allow for it: agent's reads of Codex's log and AionUi's database (`stampOf`, codex.go:2130) stand 15s at most (`reachedFor`), and library's tree memo keeps nothing whose newest file is under 3s old (`settleFor`).\n\nEach needs its own look at what a read costs while the time is recent. I'll take the internal/sessions ones once #3708 is in.\n",
